  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = \\frac{x - 4}{3}\\). If \\(f(a) = 5\\), what is the value of \\(f(2a)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "34/3"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(f(a) = 5\\) means \\(\\frac{a - 4}{3} = 5\\), so \\(a - 4 = 15\\) and \\(a = 19\\).",
    "\\(f(2a) = f(38) = \\frac{38 - 4}{3} = \\frac{34}{3}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
